#heading(level: 1, numbering: none)[Appendix A · Industry watch]
#set text(size: 9pt)
- *Frontier models ace textbook analog questions (September 2026).* The top Razavi-Bench model scored 95.50%, and the benchmark now has a simulator-assisted mode << cite('razavi_bench_2026') >>. Textbook reasoning is no longer the bottleneck; grounding, calibration and safety are what a bench tool must add, and T5 tests that head-on.
- *IBM Maximo 9.2 (June 2026)* adds an agentic assistant and an MCP server for customers' own agents << cite('ibm_mas_92_2026') >>. Asset-management platforms are becoming agent hosts, a possible route for a diagnosis engine into industrial repair depots.
- *EU AI Act transparency rules apply (2 August 2026)* << cite('ec_ip_26_1714') >>, while the Digital Omnibus moved the Annex III high-risk rules to 2 December 2027 << cite('eu_ai_omnibus_2026_1744') >>. Differential's AI disclosure is due now; high-risk duties would arise only if it were used to evaluate workers.
- *Repair rights widen for new products.* EU repair rules began to apply on 31 July 2026 << cite('ec_r2r_news_2026_07_31') >> and Texas's law took effect on 1 September 2026 << cite('tx_hb2963_2025') >>. Both help newer digital products, not the vintage analog gear Differential targets.
- *Claude Sonnet 5.5 released (28 September 2026)* << cite('claude_sonnet_5_5_overview') >>. Models change quickly, so Differential pins its model, caches responses and re-runs its safety and grounding targets on any change.

